  "proposedEffectivePlan" : "Play D3 and win the opening diamond in hand. There are eight top tricks: three clubs, two diamonds, two hearts and one spade. Seek a fourth club safely rather than risk the contract for an overtrick. Cash CA, playing dummy's C2, then lead C4 toward dummy's C7, withholding CQ even if a defender plays an honor. This concession preserves four club tricks against any 4–1 break. After losing that round, regain the lead with a side-suit winner, reach dummy with HK, cash CQ, and return to hand with a remaining side-suit ace to cash CK and the established long club. Preserve HK until it is needed for CQ, and preserve a return entry to hand afterward; coordinate these entries with any defensive return. If C7 wins, cash CQ immediately and return to hand to finish clubs. Cash the side-suit winners to reach nine tricks. If the first club reveals a 5–0 break, reassess before conceding: four club tricks are no longer assured by this line."
